---
title: "repay - Repay Borrowed Assets (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_version: check version == current_version
    q_check_version --> q_error_version: version mismatch
    q_error_version --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_version --> q_check_lock: version matches
    q_check_lock --> q_error_locked: obligation locked
    q_error_locked --> [*]: abort 770
    q_check_lock --> q_accrue_interest: obligation not locked
    q_accrue_interest --> q_calc_debt: accrue_interest(market, clock)
    q_calc_debt --> q_check_overpay: current_debt = obligation.debts[T]
    q_check_overpay --> q_cap_repay: user_coin_value > current_debt
    q_cap_repay --> q_repay: repay_amount = current_debt, return excess
    q_check_overpay --> q_repay: user_coin_value <= current_debt
    q_repay --> q_update_debt: repay_amount = min(user_coin_value, current_debt)
    q_update_debt --> q_update_pool: obligation.debts[T] -= repay_amount
    q_update_pool --> q_deposit_reserve: deposit repay_amount into lending pool
    q_deposit_reserve --> [*]: emit RepayEventV3

    note right of q_repay
        INV-001: no ObligationKey required - anyone can repay any obligation
        INV-002: repay_amount <= current_debt (excess returned to sender)
        INV-003: obligation.debts[T] decreases by exactly repay_amount
        INV-004: pool liquidity increases by repay_amount after repay
    end note
